  "findings": [
    "UDP over mesh DOES link two local meshtasticd instances: each node's DB independently listed the other. Over the process-local SimRadio they cannot hear each other at all.",
    "relay_node is the low byte of the sender's node number \u2014 confirmed here twice more (0x266cbc2b -> 0x2b, 0x2f7f90dc -> 0xdc), independently of the earlier log-based observation.",
    "The channel field carries the one-byte channel hash (8 = LongFast with the default PSK), consistent with the verified xor_fold(name) ^ xor_fold(psk).",
    "hop_limit and hop_start are ABSENT, i.e. zero. These datagrams are therefore not relayable, so this transport does not exercise the managed-flooding rebroadcast decision.",
    "The payload is the protobuf MeshPacket, not the packed LoRa frame. Nothing here settles wire layout."
  ]
}